CCLuaJIT patch 08: C stack guard
Gate: -DLUAJIT_ENABLE_CSTACKGUARD. Applies on top of 01-06 (with or without 07).

- New API: luaJIT_setcstacklimit(L, lo, hi) sets the red zone [lo, hi) of the
  C stack of the thread that runs L (lo = lowest address of the thread's stack,
  hi = lo + margin). Call it from the thread that is about to run the state.
- Every place where C code re-enters the VM checks the C stack pointer and
  raises a catchable "C stack overflow" error inside the zone: lua_call,
  lua_pcall/lua_cpcall (returned as an error status), lua_resume (LUA_ERRRUN,
  message on the coroutine, coroutine stays resumable), metamethod calls from
  lua_gettable/getfield/settable/setfield/equal/lessthan/concat and
  luaL_callmeta, parser nesting, and the coroutine.resume/wrap fast path of the
  x64 (GC64) VM (C fallback: resume returns false, msg; wrap raises).
- The guard is a range check, so a zone that belongs to another thread is
  inactive rather than wrong. Common-case cost: one compare per re-entry.
- Not guard points: the xpcall message handler call and __gc finalizer calls
  (single, bounded re-entries); lua_pcall in the zone does not call its
  message handler. global_State grows by 64 bytes (2 fields + padding: a
  16-byte shift measurably slowed coroutine switches through alignment).
- Tested: Windows x64 (native threads and JDK 21 Java threads with 1 MB
  stacks), Linux x64. The VM fast-path check exists only for x64 GC64.

